IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ia-types`
IMPORT `ia-presentation`
IMPORT `ia-terms-and-fraud`

-- Insurance Act 2015 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "A business insured has claimed for a loss. Do Parts 2-4 apply; was
--    there a qualifying breach of the duty of fair presentation and what may
--    the insurer do; is liability suspended by a breach of warranty or
--    excluded by a term or by fraud; and what must the insurer pay?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Claim case` HAS
    `the contract`                                      IS A `Contract facts`
    `the presentation`                                  IS A `Presentation`
    `what the insurer would have done`                  IS A `What the insurer would have done`
    `the money`                                         IS A `Money facts`
    `the claim`                                         IS A `Claim`
    `a breach of warranty`                              IS A MAYBE `Warranty breach`
    `a term not complied with`                          IS A MAYBE `Term non-compliance`
    `the fraud facts`                                   IS A `Fraud facts`

DECLARE `Claim position` HAS
    `Parts 2 to 4 apply`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `Parts 3 and 4 apply`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `fair presentation made`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `qualifying breach`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `remedy for the presentation`                       IS A `Remedy`
    `suspended by breach of warranty`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `excluded by non-compliance with a term`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `excluded by fraud`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `sums the insurer may recover`                      IS A NUMBER
    `amount payable on the claim`                       IS A NUMBER

@ref ss 3, 8, 10, 11, 12, 22, Sch 1 Part 1
@export default The position under the Insurance Act 2015 (UK) when a non-consumer insured claims for a loss: whether Parts 2-4 apply (ss 1, 2, 22); whether a fair presentation was made (s 3), whether there was a qualifying breach (s 8) and the insurer's remedy (Sch 1 Part 1); whether liability is suspended by a breach of warranty (s 10), excluded by non-compliance with a term the insurer may rely on (s 11), or excluded by fraud (s 12); what the insurer may recover; and the amount payable on the claim. For a consumer contract Part 2 does not apply (the 2012 Act governs disclosure; not applied here) but ss 10-12 do; for a contract entered into before 12 August 2016 the amount refuses, as the law before the Act is not encoded. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Claim case`  @desc The contract, the presentation and what the insurer would have done, the premiums and claim amounts, the day of the loss, any breach of warranty or non-compliance with a term, and the fraud facts
GIVETH A `Claim position`
`the claim position for` c MEANS
    `Claim position` WITH
        `Parts 2 to 4 apply`                            IS applies
        `Parts 3 and 4 apply`                           IS parts34
        `fair presentation made`                        IS `a fair presentation was made in` p
        `qualifying breach`                             IS `there is a qualifying breach in` p `given` w `and` x
        `remedy for the presentation`                   IS remedy
        `suspended by breach of warranty`               IS suspended
        `excluded by non-compliance with a term`        IS termExcludes
        `excluded by fraud`                             IS fraud
        `sums the insurer may recover`                  IS IF parts34 THEN `the sums the insurer may recover under` (c's `the fraud facts`) ELSE 0
        `amount payable on the claim`                   IS
            BRANCH
                IF NOT parts34 THEN REFUSE "The contract was entered into before 12 August 2016: the Insurance Act 2015 does not apply, and the law before it is not encoded."
                IF suspended OR termExcludes OR fraud THEN 0
                IF NOT applies THEN x's `the claim under the actual terms`
                IF remedy's `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims` THEN 0
                OTHERWISE remedy's `amount payable on the claim`
    WHERE
        p MEANS c's `the presentation`
        w MEANS c's `what the insurer would have done`
        x MEANS c's `the money`
        d MEANS c's `the claim`'s `the event occurred on`
        applies MEANS `Parts 2 to 4 apply to` (c's `the contract`)
        parts34 MEANS `Parts 3 and 4 apply to` (c's `the contract`)
        remedy MEANS `the remedy for the presentation in` p `given` w `and` x
        suspended MEANS
            CONSIDER c's `a breach of warranty`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST b  THEN `the breach of warranty` b `suspends liability for a loss on` d
        termExcludes MEANS
            CONSIDER c's `a term not complied with`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST t  THEN `the insurer may rely on the non-compliance in` t
        fraud MEANS `fraud excludes liability under` (c's `the fraud facts`) `for an event on` d
